  "result": "Fixed. Clamping an `IntRange` with an open bound returned a value outside the allowed range.\n\nThe cause was in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. It computed `bound - dir`, which moved the clamped value the wrong way. With `min_open=True` and min 0, clamping gave -1 instead of 1. With `max_open=True` and max 5, it gave 6 instead of 4. I changed it to `bound + dir`. Closed bounds were never affected, because they return the bound unchanged.\n\nI added two cases to `tests/test_types.py` for open-bound clamping: -3 clamps to 1 and 9 clamps to 4. `tests/test_types.py` passes (43 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't run the full suite.\n\nI didn't touch `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, which CLAUDE.md asks to update for user-visible changes. I skipped them to keep the fix minimal, so say if you want an entry added.",
